        "Top-band **AO2 marks (15/30)** go to candidates who treat the text as a **performed play** built on classical **unities of time, place, and action** (one continuous evening inside one room):\n\n- **Set Design as Psychological Exposure**: The suburban Brumley dining room is *'substantial and heavily comfortable, but not cosy and homelike'*. The coordinated adverbs expose a family rich in material assets (*'good solid furniture'*, port, cigars) yet spiritually barren.\n- **The Famous Lighting Cue**: Priestley specifies: **'The lighting should be pink and intimate until the INSPECTOR arrives, and then it should be brighter and harder.'**\n  - *'Pink and intimate'*: Literally rose-tinted self-delusion, shielding the Birlings inside a warm bourgeois bubble.\n  - *'Brighter and harder'*: Harsher interrogation-lamp / spotlight glare that strips away pretence and turns the dining room into a moral courtroom.\n- **Props with Symbolic Arcs**:\n  - **Engagement Ring**: Given in Act 1 (patriarchal alliance), handed back in Act 2 (moral independence), offered again in Act 3 and refused (*'No, not yet'*).\n  - **Port & Whisky Decanter**: Signifies wannabe aristocratic status (Birling bragging his port matches Gerald's father's) while quietly betraying Eric's secret alcoholism (*'squiffy'*).\n  - **The Photograph**: Goole insists on **'one line of inquiry at a time'**, holding the card tightly in his pocket so only one person sees it at once — controlling dramatic pace while planting the seed for Gerald's Act 3 hoax theory.\n  - **Doorbell & Telephone**: Sharp acoustic interruptions from the outside world piercing the Birlings' sealed domestic fortress.\n- **Seamless Well-Made Play Cliffhangers**:\n  - *End of Act 1*: Goole re-opens the door slowly and asks Gerald/Sheila a single monosyllable: **'Well?'** Act 2 opens on the exact same frozen tableau and word **'Well?'**, denying characters and audience any escape.\n  - *End of Act 2*: Sybil demands the child's father be severely punished; Sheila begs her to stop; the front door slams and **Eric walks in**, pale and silent, as the curtain falls.",
      diagram: `<svg viewBox="0 0 620 215" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Stagecraft architecture across Acts 1 to 3 showing lighting shift, single dining room set, prop arcs and curtain cliffhangers"><rect x="10" y="10" width="600" height="195" rx="14" fill="#1e293b"/><rect x="28" y="28" width="175" height="158" rx="10" fill="#fce7f3" stroke="#f472b6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="115" y="50" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#831843" font-family="sans-serif">Pre-Inspector</text><text x="115" y="70" font-size="11" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d174d" font-family="sans-serif">'pink and intimate'</text><text x="115" y="96" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#500724" font-family="sans-serif">Port, cigars, ring</text><text x="115" y="114" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#500724" font-family="sans-serif">'not cosy and homelike'</text><rect x="52" y="135" width="126" height="32" rx="6" fill="#be185d"/><text x="115" y="155" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-family="sans-serif">BELL RINGS SHARPLY</text><rect x="222" y="28" width="176" height="158" rx="10" fill="#fefce8" stroke="#facc15" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="310" y="50" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#713f12" font-family="sans-serif">Goole's Inquiry</text><text x="310" y="70" font-size="11" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="#854d0e" font-family="sans-serif">'brighter and harder'</text><text x="310" y="96" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#422006" font-family="sans-serif">1 photo at a time</text><text x="310" y="114" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#422006" font-family="sans-serif">Act 1-&gt;2 freeze: 'Well?'</text><text x="310" y="132" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#422006" font-family="sans-serif">Act 2 curtain: Eric enters</text><rect x="247" y="145" width="126" height="26" rx="6" fill="#ca8a04"/><text x="310" y="162" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-family="sans-serif">Ring handed back</text><rect x="417" y="28" width="175" height="158" rx="10" fill="#fee2e2" stroke="#f87171" stroke-width="2"/><text x="504" y="50" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7f1d1d" font-family="sans-serif">Act 3 Finale</text><text x="504" y="70" font-size="11" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="#991b1b" font-family="sans-serif">False Hoax Relief</text><text x="504" y="96" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#450a0a" font-family="sans-serif">Goole exits after sermon</text><text x="504" y="114" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="#450a0a" font-family="sans-serif">Birlings laugh off guilt</text><rect x="438" y="135" width="132" height="32" rx="6" fill="#dc2626"/><text x="504" y="155" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-family="sans-serif">TELEPHONE RINGS</text></svg>`,
      diagramCaption: "Priestley brackets the play with two sharp acoustic intrusions — the Act 1 doorbell and the Act 3 telephone — inside one inescapable room.",
